---
/**
 * What this site collects, which is almost nothing, and the one thing that
 * surprises people.
 *
 * THE PART THAT MATTERS is the contact form. A submission does not just sit in
 * Netlify's dashboard: `netlify/functions/shopify-subscribe.mjs` runs after
 * Netlify accepts it and creates a Shopify customer with email marketing
 * consent SUBSCRIBED. That function is deployed here and this site's Netlify
 * environment has SHOPIFY_CLIENT_ID and SHOPIFY_CLIENT_SECRET set, so it is
 * live rather than dormant — checked 2026-09-09, not assumed.
 *
 * Note ContactBlock.astro's header comment still says this site is NOT wired to
 * that function. It is stale; the function and the credentials are both here.
 * Believing it would have put a false statement about personal data on this
 * page, which is the whole reason the env was checked rather than the comment.
 *
 * The single-origin claim is measured rather than asserted: the only external
 * origins in the built HTML are the XML and schema.org NAMESPACES, which are
 * identifiers and never fetched, plus a handful of outbound credit links.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteIcon from '../components/SiteIcon.astro';
import ProsePage from '../components/ProsePage.astro';

const description =
  'What Glizzy Store collects, which is almost nothing, and what happens to your address if you send the form.';
---

<Layout title="Privacy — Glizzy Store" description={description} scripts={false}>
  <SiteIcon />
  <ProsePage heading="Privacy">
    <p>
      This is a static site. The pages were built ahead of time and are served as files. There is
      no account to make, no session, no login, and no profile of you anywhere in it.
    </p>

    <h2>Reading the site</h2>
    <p>
      No cookies, no analytics, no trackers, and no advertising. The typefaces, the scripts and
      the images all come from this domain, so this site loads nothing from anyone else. Netlify
      hosts the site and, like any web host, keeps ordinary server logs of requests made to it. That is infrastructure rather than something this site chooses to
      collect, and none of it is used to build a picture of you.
    </p>

    <h2>The shop</h2>
    <p>
      The shop reaches Shopify at the moment you add something to a cart, and not before. Your
      cart lives in your own browser's storage on this domain; it holds a cart identifier, which
      is a credential, so it is never put in a link or shared between devices. Checkout is
      Shopify's and happens on <strong>shop.vinton.land</strong>. That is the same store under a
      different name, which is why the address changes at the checkout button. What Shopify
      collects there, payment details included, is Shopify's to describe, and this site never sees
      a card number.
    </p>

    <h2>The contact form</h2>
    <p>
      Sending the form gives up three things: your name, your email address and your message. They
      are stored by Netlify and read by a person.
    </p>
    <p>
      One more thing happens, and it is the reason this page exists.
      <strong>Your email address is also added to the shop's mailing list</strong>, as a customer
      in Shopify with email marketing consent set to subscribed. So writing in with a question also
      signs you up to hear from the shop. If that is not what you wanted, every message the shop
      sends carries an unsubscribe link, and asking through the form works too.
    </p>
    <p>
      Messages are kept because they are correspondence, not data collection. Ask and yours will be
      deleted.
    </p>

    <h2>Anything else</h2>
    <p>
      This page describes what the site does today, and it is written to be checkable rather than
      reassuring. If something here does not match what you observe, that is worth saying on
      <a href="/contact/">the contact page</a>. How the site is built is in the
      <a href="/colophon/">colophon</a>, and what the shop actually sells is on
      <a href="/about/">the about page</a>.
    </p>
  </ProsePage>
</Layout>
